-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://api.z.ai/">api.z.ai<=
/a> and <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=
=3D"https://bigmodel.cn/">BigModel.cn</a>, and is compatible with Claude Co=
de and OpenClaw.</p>
<h1 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-3xl font-bold leading-[125%] py-=
3">Getting started with GLM-5.1</h1>
<h2 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-2xl font-bold leading-[125%] pb-=
2">Use GLM-5.1 with GLM Coding Plan</h2>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">Try <=
strong>GLM-5.1</strong> in your favorite coding agents=E2=80=94<strong>Clau=
de Code, OpenCode, Kilo Code, Roo Code, Cline, Droid</strong>, and more. <a=
 class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://=
docs.z.ai/devpack/overview">https://docs.z.ai/devpack/overview</a></p>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7"><stro=
ng>For GLM Coding Plan subscribers:</strong> We=E2=80=99re rolling out GLM-=
5.1 to all Coding Plan users. You can enable GLM-5.1 now by updating the mo=
del name to <code>"GLM-5.1"</code> (e.g. in <code>~/.claude/settings.json</=
code> for Claude Code). As our most capable model, GLM-5.1 consumes quota a=
t 3=C3=97 during peak hours and 2=C3=97 during off-peak hours. As a limited=
-time promotion through the end of April, off-peak usage is billed at 1=C3=
=97. (Peak hours are 14:00=E2=80=9318:00 UTC+8 (Beijing Time) daily)</p>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">Prefe=
r a GUI? We offer <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_bla=
nk" href=3D"https://zcode.z.ai/"><strong>Z Code</strong></a> =E2=80=94one i=
nterface, multiple agents, working together. Develop on remote machines ove=
r SSH, or kick off tasks from your phone and check back later.</p>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7"><stro=
ng>Start building now:</strong> <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" =
target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://z.ai/subscribe">https://z.ai/subscribe</a=
></p>
<h2 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-2xl font-bold leading-[125%] pb-=
2">Chat with GLM-5.1 on Z.ai</h2>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">GLM-5=
.1 will be available on <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=
=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://chat.z.ai/">Z.ai</a> in the coming days.</p>
<h2 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-2xl font-bold leading-[125%] pb-=
2">Serve GLM-5.1 Locally</h2>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">The m=
odel weights of GLM-5.1 are publicly available on <a class=3D"hover:text-gr=
ay-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://huggingface.co/zai-org/=
GLM-5.1">HuggingFace</a> and <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" tar=
get=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://modelscope.cn/models/ZhipuAI/GLM-5.1">ModelS=
cope</a>. For local deployment, GLM-5.1 supports inference frameworks inclu=
ding vLLM and SGLang. Comprehensive deployment instructions are available a=
t the official GitHub repository.</p>
<h1 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-3xl font-bold leading-[125%] py-=
3">Footnote</h1>
<ul class=3D"list-disc pl-6">
<li><strong>Humanity=E2=80=99s Last Exam (HLE) &amp; other reasoning tasks<=
/strong>: We evaluate with a maximum generation length of 163,840 tokens (<=
code>temperature=3D1.0, top_p=3D0.95, max_new_tokens=3D163840</code>). By d=
efault, we report the text-only subset; results marked with * are from the =
full set. We use GPT-5.2 (medium) as the judge model. For HLE-with-tools, w=
e use a maximum context length of 202,752 tokens.</li>
<li><strong>SWE-Bench Pro</strong>: We run the SWE-Bench Pro suite with Ope=
nHands using a tailored instruction prompt. Settings: <code>temperature=3D1=
</code>, <code>top_p=3D0.95</code>, <code>max_new_tokens=3D32768</code>, wi=
th a 200K context window.</li>
<li><strong>NL2Repo</strong>: We evaluated NL2Repo with <code>temperature=
=3D1.0</code>, <code>top_p=3D1.0</code>, and <code>max_new_tokens=3D32768</=
code> under 200k context. To prevent hacking, we use rule-based pre-detecti=
on for malicious commands (e.g., unauthorized pip or curl operations), foll=
owed by a model-based judgement. Malicious action is immediately intercepte=
d.</li>
<li><strong>BrowseComp</strong>: Without context management, we retain deta=
ils from the most recent 5 turns. With context management, we use the same =
discard-all strategy as GLM-5 and DeepSeek-v3.2.</li>
<li><strong>Terminal-Bench 2.0 (Terminus 2)</strong>: We evaluate with the =
Terminus framework using <code>timeout=3D3h, temperature=3D1.0, top_p=3D1.0=
, max_new_tokens=3D8192</code>, with a 200K context window. Resource limits=
 are capped at 16 CPUs and 32 GB RAM.</li>
<li><strong>Terminal-Bench 2.0 (Claude Code)</strong>: We evaluate in Claud=
e Code 2.1.69 (think mode) with <code>temperature=3D1.0, top_p=3D0.95, max_=
new_tokens=3D131072</code>. We override max_new_tokens to 128k via a transp=
arent proxy, bypassing the 64k CLI cap to restore the configurability of <c=
ode>CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS</code>. We remove wall-clock time limits,=
 while preserving per-task CPU and memory constraints. We fix environment i=
ssues introduced by Claude Code. Scores are averaged over 5 runs.</li>
<li><strong>CyberGym</strong>: We evaluate GLM-5.1 in Claude Code 2.1.56 (t=
hink mode, no web tools) with (<code>temperature=3D1.0, top_p=3D1.0, max_ne=
w_tokens=3D32000</code>), Gemini 3.1 Pro in Gemini CLI 0.36.0 with (default=
 temperature, top_p and <code>max_new_tokens=3D32000</code>), GPT-5.4 in Co=
dex CLI 0.118.0 with  (default temperature, top_p and high reasoning effort=
). All evaluations are under a 250-minute timeout per task and results are =
single-run Pass@1 over 1,507 tasks.
In evaluations of Gemini 3.1 Pro and GPT-5.4, both models sometimes identif=
ied the task as having security risks and refused to proceed, which may low=
er their scores.</li>
<li><strong>MCP-Atlas</strong>: All models were evaluated in think mode on =
the 500-task public subset with a 10-minute timeout per task. We use Gemini=
-3.0-Pro as the judge model for evaluation.</li>
<li><strong>=CF=84=C2=B3-bench</strong>: An additional prompt was added to =
the user simulator across all domains to avoid failure modes caused by user=
s ending the interaction prematurely. Banking domain uses terminal-based ag=
entic search retrieval (terminal_use). User simulator: GPT-5.2 (reasoning_e=
ffort: low), 4 trials.</li>
<li><strong>Vending Bench 2</strong>: Runs are conducted independently by <=
a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https:/=
/andonlabs.com/evals/vending-bench-2">Andon Labs</a>.</li>
<li><strong>KernelBench Level 3</strong>: Each of the 50 problems runs in a=
n isolated Docker container with one H100 GPU, limited to 1200 tool-use tur=
ns. Correctness (<code>atol=3Drtol=3D1e-4</code>) and performance are evalu=
ated against the PyTorch eager baseline in separate CUDA contexts. All solu=
tions are independently audited for benchmark exploitation by Claude Opus 4=
.6 (max effort) and GPT-5.4 (xhigh): each audit verifies the optimization d=
oes not exploit benchmark-specific behavior, works with arbitrary new input=
s, and keeps all computation on the default CUDA stream. The lower speedup =
across audits is used, with a 50=C3=97 hard cap to limit the influence of o=
utliers.</li>
